  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1242 AM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nTuesday Night-Thursday...Another shortwave trough swings into \nNorth Dakota and south-central Canada. As today's low pressure \noccludes, a secondary low pressure forms over the Dakotas and \nfollows the trough into Canada on Wednesday. A cold front will \nlag behind the new low and move into northern Iowa Wednesday \nnight before stalling over our CWA on Thursday with zonal flow \naloft. Moisture from the tropical Pacific could support \nscattered PoPs (30-60%) ahead of and along this stalling front.\n\nFriday-Sunday...The end of the week appears to be a similar \nset-up to today with the region sandwiched between a low \npressure over the Central Plains and a high pressure over the \nGreat Lakes. This will support southeasterly flow across the CWA\nwith a weak warm front along the confluence zone. Continued \nadvection of Pacific moisture keeps PoPs (30-50% coverage) \naround Friday through Saturday night. On Sunday, the longwave \ntrough over the western CONUS is likely to eject eastward into \nthe Northern Rockies, paving the way for a more active pattern \nheading into the first week of November.",
